IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er2-common`
IMPORT `er2-allocation`

-- Tests of er2-common and er2-allocation (regulations 22 to 24.3). Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the regulation
-- named beside it, and was decided before the run. One #ASSERT per line. 2026 and 2027 are not leap years; 2024 is.

§ `Test periods`

-- E1: 5 Jan to 4 Apr 2026, 27 + 28 + 31 + 4 = 90 days. QP1: 52 weeks (364 days), 1 Mar 2026 to 27 Feb 2027.
-- E1 and QP1 share 1 Mar to 4 Apr 2026: 31 + 4 = 35 days.
`er2 test E1` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5), (YearMonthDay 2026 4 4)
`er2 test QP1` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1), (YearMonthDay 2027 2 27)
-- E2 lies wholly within QP1, E3 wholly before it.
`er2 test E2` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 8 31)
`er2 test E3` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31)
-- E4: 1 Jan 2024 to 31 Dec 2025, 366 + 365 = 731 days (longer than 52 weeks); its record of employment covers R4, all of 2025 (365 days).
-- QP4 begins 1 Jul 2025; R4 and QP4 share 1 Jul to 31 Dec 2025 = 184 days.
`er2 test E4` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31)
`er2 test R4` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31)
`er2 test QP4` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)
-- E5 is exactly 364 days (52 weeks), E6 is 365; R6 is the period covered by the record of employment.
`er2 test E5` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 12 30)
`er2 test E6` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 12 31)
`er2 test R6` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 12 31)
-- E7 starts on the first day of QP1 and ends inside it; E8 starts a day before QP1; E9 is 7 days (27 Feb to 5 Mar 2027) and only its first day is in QP1.
`er2 test E7` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)
`er2 test E8` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)
`er2 test E9` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2027 2 27), (YearMonthDay 2027 3 5)

§ `er2-common - helpers`

#ASSERT `er2 the later of two days` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 5
#ASSERT `er2 the later of two days` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 5
#ASSERT `er2 the earlier of two days` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `er2 the earlier of two days` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `er2 the number of days two periods have in common` `er2 test E1` `er2 test QP1` EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `er2 the number of days two periods have in common` `er2 test QP1` `er2 test E1` EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `er2 the number of days two periods have in common` `er2 test E3` `er2 test QP1` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `er2 the number of days two periods have in common` `er2 test E9` `er2 test QP1` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `er2 the number of days two periods have in common` `er2 test E2` `er2 test QP1` EQUALS 92
#ASSERT `er2 a period lies wholly within another` `er2 test E2` `er2 test QP1`
#ASSERT NOT (`er2 a period lies wholly within another` `er2 test E1` `er2 test QP1`)
#ASSERT `er2 the week containing the day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 7)

§ `Regulation 22 - hours allocated to the qualifying period`

#ASSERT     `reg 22(1) a period of employment falls partially within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E1` `er2 test QP1`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22(1) a period of employment falls partially within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E2` `er2 test QP1`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22(1) a period of employment falls partially within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E3` `er2 test QP1`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22(1) a period of employment falls partially within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E7` `er2 test QP1`)
#ASSERT     `reg 22(1) a period of employment falls partially within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E8` `er2 test QP1`
#ASSERT     `reg 22(1) a period of employment falls partially within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E9` `er2 test QP1`
#ASSERT     `reg 22(1) a period of employment falls partially within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E4` `er2 test QP4`
-- (a): a period of 52 weeks or less (364 days) is allocated over itself; a longer one over the period the record of employment covers
#ASSERT `reg 22(1)(a) the period over which the total number of hours worked is allocated` `er2 test E5` `er2 test R6` EQUALS `er2 test E5`
#ASSERT `reg 22(1)(a) the period over which the total number of hours worked is allocated` `er2 test E6` `er2 test R6` EQUALS `er2 test R6`
#ASSERT `reg 22(1)(a) the period over which the total number of hours worked is allocated` `er2 test E4` `er2 test R4` EQUALS `er2 test R4`
-- (a), (b): 360 hours over 90 days is 4 a day; 35 days in the qualifying period is 140 hours
#ASSERT `reg 22(1)(a), (b) the hours allocated to the qualifying period, before any fraction of an hour is counted` `er2 test E1` `er2 test E1` `er2 test QP1` 360 EQUALS JUST 140
-- 100 hours over 90 days, 35 of them in the qualifying period: 3500 / 90 = 350 / 9
#ASSERT `reg 22(1)(a), (b) the hours allocated to the qualifying period, before any fraction of an hour is counted` `er2 test E1` `er2 test E1` `er2 test QP1` 100 EQUALS JUST (350 DIVIDED BY 9)
-- over 52 weeks: 1825 hours over R4's 365 days is 5 a day; 184 days in the qualifying period is 920 hours
#ASSERT `reg 22(1)(a), (b) the hours allocated to the qualifying period, before any fraction of an hour is counted` `er2 test E4` `er2 test R4` `er2 test QP4` 1825 EQUALS JUST 920
-- reg 22(1) does not decide where the period is not partially within the qualifying period
#ASSERT `reg 22(1)(a), (b) the hours allocated to the qualifying period, before any fraction of an hour is counted` `er2 test E2` `er2 test E2` `er2 test QP1` 500 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): a fraction of an hour is counted as a whole hour
#ASSERT `reg 22(2) a fraction of an hour counted as a whole hour` (350 DIVIDED BY 9) EQUALS 39
#ASSERT `reg 22(2) a fraction of an hour counted as a whole hour` 38 EQUALS 38
#ASSERT `reg 22(2) a fraction of an hour counted as a whole hour` 0.01 EQUALS 1
-- the whole rule, no evidence: 140 exactly, and 39 for the fraction
#ASSERT `reg 22 the hours of insurable employment counted within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E1` `er2 test E1` `er2 test QP1` 360 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 140
#ASSERT `reg 22 the hours of insurable employment counted within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E1` `er2 test E1` `er2 test QP1` 100 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 39
#ASSERT `reg 22 the hours of insurable employment counted within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E4` `er2 test R4` `er2 test QP4` 1825 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 920
-- one day of seven in the qualifying period: 70 hours / 7 days * 1 day = 10
#ASSERT `reg 22 the hours of insurable employment counted within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E9` `er2 test E9` `er2 test QP1` 70 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 10
-- evidence of the hours actually worked governs, whatever the allocation would give
#ASSERT `reg 22 the hours of insurable employment counted within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E1` `er2 test E1` `er2 test QP1` 360 (JUST 77) EQUALS JUST 77
-- wholly within or wholly outside the qualifying period: the regulation does not decide
#ASSERT `reg 22 the hours of insurable employment counted within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E2` `er2 test E2` `er2 test QP1` 500 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 22 the hours of insurable employment counted within the claimant's qualifying period` `er2 test E3` `er2 test E3` `er2 test QP1` 500 (JUST 12) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 23 - which method allocates a payment`

-- (b): the ten always-listed items, and wages in lieu of notice and vacation pay only when not paid in respect of a pay period (fork F4)
#ASSERT     `reg 23(1)(b) the remuneration is one of the items listed in paragraph (b)` `er2 overtime pay` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period`
#ASSERT     `reg 23(1)(b) the remuneration is one of the items listed in paragraph (b)` `er2 separation payments` `er2 not paid in respect of a pay period`
#ASSERT     `reg 23(1)(b) the remuneration is one of the items listed in paragraph (b)` `er2 wages in lieu of notice` `er2 not paid in respect of a pay period`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(1)(b) the remuneration is one of the items listed in paragraph (b)` `er2 wages in lieu of notice` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period`)
#ASSERT     `reg 23(1)(b) the remuneration is one of the items listed in paragraph (b)` `er2 vacation pay` `er2 not paid in respect of a pay period`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(1)(b) the remuneration is one of the items listed in paragraph (b)` `er2 vacation pay` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for a period of leave`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(1)(b) the remuneration is one of the items listed in paragraph (b)` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 not paid in respect of a pay period`)
-- (1): the method
#ASSERT `reg 23(1) the method of allocating a payment under paragraphs (a) to (c)` `er2 overtime pay` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` EQUALS JUST `er2 proportionately over the pay period in which it is paid`
#ASSERT `reg 23(1) the method of allocating a payment under paragraphs (a) to (c)` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` EQUALS JUST `er2 to the pay period in proportion to the hours worked during each day of the period`
#ASSERT `reg 23(1) the method of allocating a payment under paragraphs (a) to (c)` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for a period of leave` EQUALS JUST `er2 to the period of leave at the rate at which the period was compensated`
#ASSERT `reg 23(1) the method of allocating a payment under paragraphs (a) to (c)` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for a period of leave as a lump sum calculated on a basis other than the length of the leave` EQUALS JUST `er2 proportionately over the whole period of leave`
#ASSERT `reg 23(1) the method of allocating a payment under paragraphs (a) to (c)` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 not paid in respect of a pay period` EQUALS JUST `er2 proportionately over the pay period in which it is paid`
#ASSERT `reg 23(1) the method of allocating a payment under paragraphs (a) to (c)` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period but neither for work performed during it nor for a period of leave` EQUALS NOTHING
-- vacation pay paid in respect of a pay period of leave is (a)(ii), not (b); wages in lieu paid in respect of a pay period for work are (a)(i)
#ASSERT `reg 23(1) the method of allocating a payment under paragraphs (a) to (c)` `er2 vacation pay` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for a period of leave` EQUALS JUST `er2 to the period of leave at the rate at which the period was compensated`
#ASSERT `reg 23(1) the method of allocating a payment under paragraphs (a) to (c)` `er2 wages in lieu of notice` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` EQUALS JUST `er2 to the pay period in proportion to the hours worked during each day of the period`
-- (d)
#ASSERT     `reg 23(1)(d) the unpaid remuneration is allocated as if it had actually been paid in the normal course of business` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(1)(d) the unpaid remuneration is allocated as if it had actually been paid in the normal course of business` FALSE)
-- (1.1): only a paragraph (b) payment is moved, and only for a person on unpaid leave, who quit, or was terminated or laid off
#ASSERT     `reg 23(1.1) the remuneration referred to in paragraph (1)(b) is allocated over the last pay period for which regular pay is paid` TRUE `er2 bonuses` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(1.1) the remuneration referred to in paragraph (1)(b) is allocated over the last pay period for which regular pay is paid` FALSE `er2 bonuses` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(1.1) the remuneration referred to in paragraph (1)(b) is allocated over the last pay period for which regular pay is paid` TRUE `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 not paid in respect of a pay period`)
-- (2), (3)
#ASSERT     `reg 23(2) the insurable earnings are allocated over the term of the contract` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(2) the insurable earnings are allocated over the term of the contract` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(2) the insurable earnings are allocated over the term of the contract` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT     `reg 23(3) the insurable earnings are allocated over the shorter of the period of employment and the last 52 weeks` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT     `reg 23(3) the insurable earnings are allocated over the shorter of the period of employment and the last 52 weeks` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(3) the insurable earnings are allocated over the shorter of the period of employment and the last 52 weeks` FALSE FALSE)
-- (3): the shorter of the period of employment and 52 weeks (364 days), less the weeks of unpaid leave for a reason in subsection 12(3)
#ASSERT `reg 23(3) the number of days over which the insurable earnings are allocated` 400 0 EQUALS JUST 364
#ASSERT `reg 23(3) the number of days over which the insurable earnings are allocated` 100 0 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `reg 23(3) the number of days over which the insurable earnings are allocated` 400 2 EQUALS JUST 350
#ASSERT `reg 23(3) the number of days over which the insurable earnings are allocated` 100 3 EQUALS JUST 79
#ASSERT `reg 23(3) the number of days over which the insurable earnings are allocated` 14 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 23(3) the number of days over which the insurable earnings are allocated` 14 3 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4)
#ASSERT `reg 23(4) the number of days over which the insurable earnings are allocated` 400 EQUALS 364
#ASSERT `reg 23(4) the number of days over which the insurable earnings are allocated` 364 EQUALS 364
#ASSERT `reg 23(4) the number of days over which the insurable earnings are allocated` 365 EQUALS 364
#ASSERT `reg 23(4) the number of days over which the insurable earnings are allocated` 100 EQUALS 100
-- (4): none of (1) to (3) applies
#ASSERT     `reg 23(4) none of subsections (1) to (3) applies to the insurable earnings` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period but neither for work performed during it nor for a period of leave` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(4) none of subsections (1) to (3) applies to the insurable earnings` `er2 overtime pay` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(4) none of subsections (1) to (3) applies to the insurable earnings` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period but neither for work performed during it nor for a period of leave` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(4) none of subsections (1) to (3) applies to the insurable earnings` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period but neither for work performed during it nor for a period of leave` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- (5)
#ASSERT     `reg 23(5) the employer may estimate the insurable earnings for the pay period` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(5) the employer may estimate the insurable earnings for the pay period` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(5) the employer may estimate the insurable earnings for the pay period` FALSE TRUE)

§ `Regulation 23 - the method that governs, in the encoding's order (fork F5)`

-- args: item, basis, on unpaid leave or quit or terminated or laid off, fixed-term contract, earnings not paid regularly, solely commissions, salary and irregular commissions
#ASSERT `reg 23 the method of allocating insurable earnings` `er2 overtime pay` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the pay period in which it is paid`
#ASSERT `reg 23 the method of allocating insurable earnings` `er2 bonuses` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the last pay period for which regular salary, wages or commissions are paid`
-- (1.1) moves only paragraph (b): remuneration under paragraph (c) stays with the pay period in which it is paid
#ASSERT `reg 23 the method of allocating insurable earnings` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 not paid in respect of a pay period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the pay period in which it is paid`
#ASSERT `reg 23 the method of allocating insurable earnings` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the term of the contract`
-- (2) wins over (1) and (1.1): "regardless of the basis on which they are paid"
#ASSERT `reg 23 the method of allocating insurable earnings` `er2 overtime pay` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the term of the contract`
#ASSERT `reg 23 the method of allocating insurable earnings` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the shorter of the period of employment and the last 52 weeks, excluding weeks of unpaid leave for a reason in subsection 12(3) of the Act`
#ASSERT `reg 23 the method of allocating insurable earnings` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the shorter of the period of employment and the last 52 weeks, excluding weeks of unpaid leave for a reason in subsection 12(3) of the Act`
-- (2) and (3) both apply: the text does not rank them; the encoding takes (2)
#ASSERT `reg 23 the method of allocating insurable earnings` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the term of the contract`
-- (4): none of (1) to (3)
#ASSERT `reg 23 the method of allocating insurable earnings` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period but neither for work performed during it nor for a period of leave` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er2 proportionately over the shorter of the period of employment and the last 52 weeks`
-- a fixed-term contract paid regularly, or irregular pay on an open-ended contract, is not (2)
#ASSERT `reg 23 the method of allocating insurable earnings` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er2 to the pay period in proportion to the hours worked during each day of the period`
#ASSERT `reg 23 the method of allocating insurable earnings` `er2 remuneration not listed in paragraph 23(1)(b)` `er2 paid in respect of a pay period for work performed during the pay period` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `er2 to the pay period in proportion to the hours worked during each day of the period`

§ `Regulation 23 - the arithmetic of the methods`

-- "proportionately": 3 days of a 10-day period carry 3/10 of 1000
#ASSERT `reg 23 the part of an amount allocated proportionately to a stretch of days` 1000 3 10 EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `reg 23 the part of an amount allocated proportionately to a stretch of days` 1000 10 10 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `reg 23 the part of an amount allocated proportionately to a stretch of days` 700 1 7 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `reg 23 the part of an amount allocated proportionately to a stretch of days` 1000 3 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a)(i): 700 over a pay period of 40 hours, 8 of them on the day
#ASSERT `reg 23(1)(a)(i) the part of the remuneration allocated to a day in proportion to the hours worked` 700 8 40 EQUALS JUST 140
#ASSERT `reg 23(1)(a)(i) the part of the remuneration allocated to a day in proportion to the hours worked` 700 0 40 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `reg 23(1)(a)(i) the part of the remuneration allocated to a day in proportion to the hours worked` 700 8 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a)(ii): 14 days of leave at 95.50 a day
#ASSERT `reg 23(1)(a)(ii) the part of the remuneration allocated to a period of leave at the rate at which it was compensated` 95.5 14 EQUALS 1337

§ `Regulation 24 - earnings allocated to a week`

-- PE: Wed 4 Mar to Tue 17 Mar 2026, 14 days. W1: Sun 1 Mar to Sat 7 Mar (shares 4 days with PE). W3: Sun 8 Mar to Sat 14 Mar (shares 7).
-- WQ: a wide qualifying period. 2800 earned over 14 days is 200 a day.
`er2 test PE` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 17)
`er2 test W1` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 7)
`er2 test W3` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 8), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 14)
`er2 test W4` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 22), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 28)
`er2 test WQ` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 8 30)
`er2 test PE2` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5)
`er2 test WQ late` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5), (YearMonthDay 2027 3 4)
-- args: period of employment, the week, the qualifying period, earnings on the record, lay-off or separation earnings, evidence of earnings actually earned in the week
#ASSERT `reg 24 the insurable earnings allocated to the week` `er2 test PE` `er2 test W1` `er2 test WQ` 2800 0 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 800
-- without the 700 of separation pay: (2800 - 700) * 4 / 14 = 600
#ASSERT `reg 24 the insurable earnings allocated to the week` `er2 test PE` `er2 test W1` `er2 test WQ` 2800 700 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 600
-- evidence of what was actually earned in the week governs
#ASSERT `reg 24 the insurable earnings allocated to the week` `er2 test PE` `er2 test W1` `er2 test WQ` 2800 700 (JUST 450) EQUALS JUST 450
-- the whole week W3 is inside the period of employment, which extends beyond it: 7 days of 14
#ASSERT `reg 24 the insurable earnings allocated to the week` `er2 test PE` `er2 test W3` `er2 test WQ` 2800 0 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 1400
-- the period of employment lies wholly within the week: reg 24 does not apply
#ASSERT `reg 24 the insurable earnings allocated to the week` `er2 test PE2` `er2 test W1` `er2 test WQ` 800 0 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the period of employment does not touch the week
#ASSERT `reg 24 the insurable earnings allocated to the week` `er2 test PE` `er2 test W4` `er2 test WQ` 2800 0 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the week is not included in the qualifying period
#ASSERT `reg 24 the insurable earnings allocated to the week` `er2 test PE` `er2 test W1` `er2 test WQ late` 2800 0 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 24.1 - lay-off and separation earnings`

-- the lesser of the actual amount and A x 0.18
#ASSERT `reg 24.1 the insurable earnings paid or payable by reason of lay-off or separation that are counted` 5000 20000 EQUALS 3600
#ASSERT `reg 24.1 the insurable earnings paid or payable by reason of lay-off or separation that are counted` 3000 20000 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `reg 24.1 the insurable earnings paid or payable by reason of lay-off or separation that are counted` 3600 20000 EQUALS 3600
#ASSERT `reg 24.1 the insurable earnings paid or payable by reason of lay-off or separation that are counted` 3600.01 20000 EQUALS 3600
#ASSERT `reg 24.1 the insurable earnings paid or payable by reason of lay-off or separation that are counted` 5000 0 EQUALS 0

§ `Regulation 24.2 - repealed`

#ASSERT `regulation 24.2 - repealed, and therefore not encoded` EQUALS "24.2 [Repealed, SOR/2013-45, s. 3]"

§ `Regulation 24.3 - a self-employed person's excluded earnings`

`er2 test QP24` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2025 10 5), (YearMonthDay 2026 10 3)
-- args: lost by misconduct, left without just cause, day earned, qualifying period, first day of a prior benefit period (if any)
#ASSERT     `reg 24.3 the insurable earnings are not taken into account in the rate of weekly benefits of a self-employed person` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) `er2 test QP24` NOTHING
#ASSERT     `reg 24.3 the insurable earnings are not taken into account in the rate of weekly benefits of a self-employed person` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) `er2 test QP24` NOTHING
-- (b): earned in the qualifying period before the prior benefit period began on 1 Mar 2026
#ASSERT     `reg 24.3 the insurable earnings are not taken into account in the rate of weekly benefits of a self-employed person` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) `er2 test QP24` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1))
-- earned on the very day the prior benefit period began: not "before" it
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 24.3 the insurable earnings are not taken into account in the rate of weekly benefits of a self-employed person` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) `er2 test QP24` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 24.3 the insurable earnings are not taken into account in the rate of weekly benefits of a self-employed person` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) `er2 test QP24` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)))
-- no prior benefit period: limb (b) cannot apply
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 24.3 the insurable earnings are not taken into account in the rate of weekly benefits of a self-employed person` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) `er2 test QP24` NOTHING)
-- earned before the qualifying period began: not "in the qualifying period"
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 24.3 the insurable earnings are not taken into account in the rate of weekly benefits of a self-employed person` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) `er2 test QP24` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)))
